Subject: [PATCH 06847/11362] ARC round-3 (codex): tu93 FULL CLEAR, L6 -> L9
 (+3)

First win of the round-3 breadth campaign against the 15 remaining
unsolved games. tu93 -- a game with a long, well-documented history of
near-misses this session (v19's "richest adversary dossier... genuine
two-lock wall", broken open in round 2 to L6) -- live-won all three
remaining levels in a single session.

L7: the color-13 direction-marked runner is dormant until the player
enters its line, then traverses the maze one node per successful move.
L8: requires deliberately ACTIVATING the L7 runner as a tool (not just a
hazard), retreating around a cleared charger loop, and returning with a
safe lead. L9 (terminal level): three autonomous bouncing patrollers plus
a charger-clearing dependency (clear a lower vertical charger sideways,
then the goal-line charger from below, then enter the goal -- entering
directly gets fired through and killed).

The source agent honestly flagged the win as reproduction_verified=false
(no budget left for a dedicated gate after the live-replay confirmation
through action 186), despite the live win, a deterministic fresh-prefix
replay, and a post-win empty terminal frame. Per this project's
independent-verification discipline, the outer loop never trusts a
self-reported win: ran 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via the fixed
resolver before recording anything -- all 5 confirmed reached_level=9 AND
state=GameState.WIN. tu93 is a confirmed full clear.

reproducible_total_levels: 138 -> 141 (verified against a fresh sum).

